the Royal Yacht Britannia is shipped one  of the world's most famous families  across the seas for 40 years it offers a  personal history like few other  attractions it carried the British royal  family for state visits and holidays  Charles and Diana's honeymoon and was  even used in a refugee rescue in the  Yemen retired in Scotland's capital  Edinburgh the Britannia was  recommissioned as a top visitor  destination now with an audio tour  available in 27 different languages its  potential is being maximized the vested  economy is worth 11 billion pounds to  Scotland employs over 300,000 people I'm  switch hugely important those arguing  for Scotland to remain in the UK say  attractions like the Britannia are at  risk from independence the UK was the  eighth largest tourist destination in  the world in 2013 so will Scotland  jeopardize those extending holidays from  places like London with its open borders  and a shared currency those voting yes  counter by saying Scotland will be even  more visible on the international stage  and could in fact attract more  international flights by cutting  passenger duty and reducing taxes on  tourists whatever the result the real  damage could be done by Scotland's  biggest group of visitors eighty-two  percent of the visitors to Scotland are  from the united kingdom however the  international visitor is very important  because they spend double the amount  that a UK Vista does if people from the  UK feel antagonized by Scotland  separation the tourism industry north of  the border will have to work to keep  their big-spending visitors from  elsewhere staying longer Tom Gibson  Bloomberg
 

